rupam output exception

As a special exception, you may create a larger work that contains part or
all of the output of rupam, including the runtime support code that rupam
copies into the R, Python and other scripts it generates, and distribute that
work under terms of your choice, so long as that work isn't itself a compiler
or code generator that uses rupam's runtime support code as its own runtime
support code. Alternatively, if you modify or redistribute rupam's runtime
support code itself, you may (at your option) remove this special exception,
which will cause that code and the resulting rupam output to be licensed
under the GNU General Public License without this special exception.

This special exception is an additional permission under section 7 of the
GNU General Public License, version 3. It was added by Visruth Srimath
Kandali in rupam 0.1, following the exception in GNU Bison 2.2.
